Revision history for App-codefork

{{$NEXT}}
  - Add CLAUDE.md with project guidance for AI assistants.
  - Ship a LICENSE file in the distribution.
  - bin/codefork carries its own $VERSION.
  - Continuous integration runs on SimpiCI instead of Travis: a thin GitHub
    Actions workflow delegates to the SimpiCI reusable workflow with the
    shared [@Author::GETTY] provider, which runs a dzil test job for each
    supported Perl version (5.22 through 5.44).
  - The SUPPORT section of the codefork man page is generated by the
    distribution bundle.
  - codefork refuses, before writing anything, a plan that would overwrite a
    file: a rename onto an existing file, two files renamed to the same
    path, or two files swapping names. The diff refuses it the same way.
    When one rename frees a path for another, they are applied in a safe
    order.
  - codefork output writes the diff as raw bytes, so a diff of non-ASCII
    content applies with patch -p1.
  - apply removes the directories a rename left empty. An empty directory
    whose name matches a rule is renamed and shown in the diff.
  - The word rule (from%to) also replaces a word at the start or end of a
    file and the second of two words separated by a single character.
  - The config file is never rewritten or renamed, even when it lies inside
    the tree, as the default fork.conf does.
  - apply writes new content into the existing file, so owner, group, mode,
    hard links, ACLs and extended attributes are kept; docker run ... apply
    leaves no root-owned files on the host. A failed write restores the
    original from a backup and names it. Directories created for a rename
    take the mode and, where permitted, the owner and group of the directory
    they replace. A file to rewrite that is not writable is refused before
    anything is written.
  - codefork refuses, before writing anything, a rename that needs a
    directory where a file is, or where another file is renamed to.
  - bin/codefork no longer adds <bindir>/../lib to the module search path,
    so an installed codefork cannot load a different or stale App::codefork
    from there. From a checkout, run it as perl -Ilib bin/codefork.
  - When codefork refuses a plan it prints only the refusal and exits non-
    zero.

1.000     2026-03-06 17:14:40Z
    - BREAKING: New command-line interface, old --config/--dir/--debug flags removed
    - Diff-based workflow: preview changes before applying (safe by default)
    - New commands: apply, output (default: show diff)
    - Default config file: fork.conf (no --config flag needed)
    - Debug output via CODEFORK_DEBUG=1 environment variable
    - Replaced IO::All with Path::Tiny
    - Replaced MooX::Options with positional argument parsing
    - Removed File::chdir dependency
    - Added Text::Diff for unified diff generation

